// Title: ETW Trace Evasion Activity
// ID: a238b5d0-ce2d-4414-a676-7a531b3d13d6
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: @neu5ron, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-03-22
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1070, attack.t1685, car.2016-04-002
// Description: Detects command line activity that tries to clear or disable any ETW trace log which could be a sign of logging evasion.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "cl" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "/Trace")) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "clear-log" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "/Trace")) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "sl" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "/e:false")) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "set-log" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "/e:false")) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "logman" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "update" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "trace" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "--p" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "-ets")) OR (src.process.cmdline containsCIS "Remove-EtwTraceProvider") OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "Set-EtwTraceProvider" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "0x11")))
